// Synthetic per-zone fragment: the zone statement a nameserver that keeps one
// file per zone puts in each of them. What this fixture exercises is the COUNT
// of inlined fragments, but it carries a real zone so the verdict the test
// asserts is a verdict about a zone that was parsed.
//
// Ruling LR-15: every one of the hundred includes pulls in THIS file, so the
// hundred zone statements all carry the same name, and named refuses a
// duplicate zone name at load. That is deliberate and is the price of a cap
// fixture that needs a hundred fragments without a hundred files: this model
// does not judge duplicate zone names, so the count is what is under test. A
// duplicate-zone note belongs to a later plan, not to this fixture.
zone "example.org" IN {
	type master;
	file "/var/named/example.org.zone";
};
